      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>layering the \"grounding moments\" on top of a burning house feels like a joke. i know people say to focus on the small things, but the small things dont matter if the whole system is broken. it feels less like \"feeling overwhelmed\" and more like just... seeing the truth. if the end is inevitable, why are we all just pretending that we're supposed to keep performing these little roles and staying happy? it feels irrational to fight for a future that isn't actually coming.",
